  "goodToKnow": "Der Mönch is a monk, living in a Kloster (monastery); a nun is die Nonne. The city of München takes its name from monks: bei den Mönchen. Its coat of arms shows a small monk, das Münchner Kindl. Martin Luther began as an Augustinian monk in Erfurt. Many famous German beers, like Andechser and Weihenstephaner, have monastic roots. The Swiss mountain Mönch stands between the Eiger and the Jungfrau. Plural: die Mönche."
